: Gender, Race, Resistance in a Brooklyn Drug Market</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>Oxford: Clarendon Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Surratt</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Inciardi</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kurtz</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiley</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sex work and drug use in a subculture of violence</article-title><source>Crime &#x00026; Delinquency</source><year>2004</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>59</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/0011128703258875</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Neaigus</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An economy of risk: resource acquisition strategies of inner city women who use drugs</article-title><source>International J Drug Policy</source><year>2002</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>409</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0955-3959(02)00119-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aitken</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Higgs</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelsall</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerger</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The impact of a police crackdown on a street drug scene: evidence from the street</article-title><source>International J Drug Policy</source><year>2002</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>198</lpage>